// NOTE (Soong analysis, 2026-10-31): REMOVED module vendor.qti.hardware.camera.postproc@1.0_vendor.
// It declared stem: "vendor.qti.hardware.camera.postproc@1.0" (soc_specific -> /vendor), but the
// BASE already provides vendor/qcom/opensource/interfaces/camera/postproc/1.0 -- its android_vendor
// variant installs the SAME path, so Soong failed with:
//   packaging conflict at lib64/vendor.qti.hardware.camera.postproc@1.0.so
// Same class as commit c97abc1 (removed base-provided librmnetctl + libstdc++). Consumers that
// referenced the base name (line ~9472) keep working; only our duplicate is gone.
// LINT GAP FOUND: C14/C64 compare module NAMES, but the collision is on the INSTALLED FILENAME
// (stem/name), so a suffixed module with a shared stem slips through. New rule C82 covers it.

